{% block section_0 %}
<p>
  Marathi (मराठी) is the official language of Maharashtra — home to Mumbai, India's financial capital, and Pune, one of its fastest-growing tech cities. With approximately 95 million native speakers, Marathi is the third most spoken language in India and the 15th most spoken language in the world.<br>
  The Marathi-speaking market is strategically significant beyond its speaker count: Maharashtra generates roughly 14–15% of India's GDP, hosts the headquarters of major Indian and multinational corporations, and has a rapidly growing middle class with strong digital adoption.<br>
  This guide covers what you need to know to build a Marathi-language website that connects authentically with Maharashtra's sophisticated digital audience.
</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_1_1 %}
<p>
  Marathi has less regional variation in its written standard than languages like Chinese or Spanish, but register and context matter significantly:
</p>
<ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
  <li><strong>Standard Written Marathi (Pratishtit Marathi):</strong> The formal register used in government, journalism, and professional communications. Uses Devanagari script — the same script as Hindi, but with distinct Marathi characters and vocabulary.</li>
  <li><strong>Mumbai Marathi:</strong> The urban spoken register of Mumbai — heavily influenced by Hindi and English. "Mumbaiya" Marathi is understood across the state but is perceived as informal. Business web content should use standard Pratishtit Marathi.</li>
  <li><strong>Distinct from Hindi:</strong> Despite sharing the Devanagari script, Marathi is a different language from Hindi — with distinct vocabulary, grammar, and pronunciation. Content written in Hindi and presented as Marathi is immediately noticeable and off-putting. Native Marathi speaker review is essential.</li>
  <li><strong>Marathi vs. Hindi pride:</strong> Maharashtrians have strong linguistic pride. A genuinely Marathi website — not a Hindi website with a Marathi header — is the correct approach for this audience.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Set <code>&lt;html lang="mr"&gt;</code>. Marathi uses the Devanagari script — Devanagari-supporting fonts are required.
</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_1_2 %}
<p>
  Marathi-speaking Maharashtra operates within India's open internet environment — the same technical considerations apply as for Hindi:
</p>
<div style="background:#fff4f4; padding:16px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid #f9a8a8; margin-bottom:24px;">
  <p style="font-weight:bold; color:#c53030; margin-bottom:8px;">❌ Key technical considerations for Maharashtra</p>
  <ul style="list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0;">
    <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">· Devanagari font files must cover Marathi-specific characters — some Devanagari fonts optimized for Hindi may miss Marathi-specific conjuncts and characters</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">· Page performance on mobile is critical — while Mumbai has fast 4G/5G, a significant Marathi-speaking population lives in smaller cities and rural Maharashtra</li>
    <li>· Search optimization must account for Marathi-specific search terms — don't assume Hindi keyword research applies to Marathi queries</li>
  </ul>
</div>
<p>
  Mumbai specifically has some of the fastest mobile internet in India. But Pune, Nagpur, Nashik, and rural Maharashtra have more variable connectivity. Design for the broader Maharashtra audience, not just Mumbai.
</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_1_3 %}
<p>
  Marathi-language websites targeting Indian audiences fall under the same legal frameworks as the broader Indian market:
</p>
<ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px; margin-bottom: 24px;">
  <li><strong>Digital Personal Data Protection Act (DPDPA) 2023:</strong> India's data protection law applies — same as for Hindi-language services. Explicit consent for data collection, privacy policy accessible in Marathi, and data breach notification obligations.</li>
  <li><strong>IT Act and Consumer Protection Rules:</strong> E-commerce entities targeting Indian consumers must comply with Consumer Protection (E-Commerce) Rules — including visible return policies, grievance officer contact, and product origin disclosure.</li>
  <li><strong>Maharashtra-specific regulations:</strong> Maharashtra has some state-specific business regulations, particularly in real estate (MahaRERA) and food safety (FSSAI for food businesses). Display any applicable state or central government registrations prominently.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_2_1 %}
<p>
  Marathi-speaking Maharashtra audiences have specific content expectations shaped by the state's strong educational culture and business-savvy population:
</p>
<ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
  <li><strong>Quality Marathi content is scarce:</strong> Like Bengali, high-quality Marathi web content is relatively rare. Businesses that invest in well-written, professionally produced Marathi content stand out in an underserved content landscape.</li>
  <li><strong>Balanced bilingualism:</strong> The Marathi-speaking urban audience (particularly in Mumbai and Pune) is highly bilingual in Hindi and English. Many professional Marathis prefer English for technical or business content but respond warmly to Marathi for culturally resonant messaging — festivals, family, community contexts.</li>
  <li><strong>Maharashtra identity:</strong> Marathi cultural identity is strong — references to Marathi culture, Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj, Ganesh Chaturthi, and Marathi literature build authentic cultural connection. Using Marathi for important messages signals respect for the audience's identity.</li>
  <li><strong>WhatsApp for business:</strong> WhatsApp dominates business communication in Maharashtra — same as the broader India pattern. A WhatsApp Business button is essential.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_2_2 %}
<p>
  <strong>Google dominates search in Maharashtra with approximately 98% market share.</strong> Marathi-specific SEO nuances:
</p>
<ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
  <li><strong>Marathi voice search:</strong> Voice search in Marathi is growing rapidly — particularly for local queries ("जवळचे हॉटेल" — nearby restaurants) and conversational searches. Google's Marathi language support has improved significantly.</li>
  <li><strong>Marathi keyword research:</strong> Use Google Keyword Planner filtered to Maharashtra state. Marathi search terms differ from Hindi equivalents — "website" is "संकेतस्थळ" in formal Marathi but many users search using the English term. Cover both.</li>
  <li><strong>Google Discover in Marathi:</strong> Google Discover serves Marathi-language content to Marathi-language users in Maharashtra. Quality Marathi content can generate significant Discover traffic.</li>
  <li><strong>Local SEO for Maharashtra:</strong> Google Business Profile in Marathi is important for businesses with physical presence in Maharashtra cities. Reviews in Marathi from local customers carry local SEO weight.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_2_3 %}
<p>
  Server location for Marathi-language websites follows the same India recommendations as Hindi:
</p>
<p>
  AWS Mumbai (ap-south-1) is the optimal choice — it is physically located in Mumbai and provides sub-5ms latency to Pune, Nagpur, and other Maharashtra cities. Google Cloud Mumbai is equally appropriate. For the lowest possible latency within Maharashtra, Mumbai-region hosting is unambiguously the right choice.
</p>
<p>
  Domain choice: <code>.in</code> or <code>.co.in</code> signal Indian presence. <code>.com</code> is broadly accepted. For Maharashtra-specifically-targeted businesses, a <code>.co.in</code> or <code>.in</code> domain paired with Mumbai hosting and Marathi content creates a strong local presence signal.
</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_3_1 %}
<p>
  Marathi cultural color associations blend Hindu tradition, Maharashtra's royal Maratha heritage, and modern Indian design:
</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">🟠 <strong>Saffron/orange:</strong> The color of the Maratha Empire and closely associated with Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj and Maharashtra's cultural identity. Also Hindu auspiciousness. Powerful for Marathi cultural contexts.</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">🟡 <strong>Yellow/gold:</strong> Prosperity, Ganesh Chaturthi (Maharashtra's biggest festival), and celebration. Yellow marigold (झेंडूचं फूल) is the quintessential Marathi festive color — deeply associated with Ganesh Puja.</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">🔴 <strong>Red:</strong> Auspiciousness, marriage, and celebration in Hindu Marathi culture. The sindoor (vermillion) red and the bridal tradition give red strong positive cultural associations.</li>
  <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">🟢 <strong>Green:</strong> Nature, growth, and freshness. Widely used in wellness, food, and agricultural contexts — important for Maharashtra's agricultural sector.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_3_2 %}
<p>
  Marathi uses the Devanagari script — the same script as Hindi, but requiring font support for Marathi-specific characters. Not all Devanagari fonts cover the full Marathi character set.
</p>
<div style="background:#f1f5f9; padding:12px; border-radius:4px; font-family:monospace; margin-bottom:16px;">
  font-family: "Noto Sans Devanagari", "Poppins", "Hind", sans-serif;
</div>
<p>
  "Noto Sans Devanagari" provides the most comprehensive Marathi Unicode coverage and is the safest choice. Verify that your chosen font explicitly supports Marathi conjuncts — some Devanagari fonts are designed primarily for Hindi and may render certain Marathi-specific conjunct characters incorrectly.
</p>
<p>
  Body text at <strong>16–18px</strong>, line-height <strong>1.8–2.0</strong>. Same requirements as Hindi — Devanagari script needs generous line spacing for the horizontal bar (shirorékha) to breathe. Marathi text length is broadly similar to Hindi equivalents.
</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_3_3 %}
<p>
  Marathi web design follows broadly similar patterns to Hindi-language Indian web design, with some Maharashtra-specific aesthetic elements:
</p>
<ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
  <li><strong>Festival-aware design:</strong> Ganesh Chaturthi is Maharashtra's defining cultural moment — a 10-day celebration that shapes commerce, community, and emotion across the state. Businesses that acknowledge Ganesh Chaturthi (and Gudi Padwa, the Marathi new year) in their seasonal design signal genuine Maharashtra identity.</li>
  <li><strong>Mumbai financial district expectations:</strong> For B2B services targeting Mumbai's corporate market, design quality expectations are high — comparable to any major global financial center. Clean, professional, international-standard design is expected.</li>
  <li><strong>Agricultural and rural Maharashtra:</strong> For businesses serving Maharashtra's farming communities and smaller cities, accessible design with clear product information and visible contact details is more important than visual sophistication.</li>
  <li><strong>Trust signals:</strong> Maharashtra state registrations, FSSAI marks, and government certifications displayed prominently build credibility with both urban and rural Maharashtra audiences.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_4_1 %}
<p>
  Contact preferences in Maharashtra follow the broader Indian pattern, with some Maharashtra-specific nuances:
</p>
<ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
  <li><strong>WhatsApp Business:</strong> The primary contact channel for business communication in Maharashtra — same as India broadly. A floating WhatsApp button is the standard and expected CTA.</li>
  <li><strong>Phone contact in Marathi:</strong> For businesses targeting non-metro Maharashtra, offering Marathi-language phone support significantly increases accessibility and trust. A visible Mumbai/Maharashtra area code (+91 22 for Mumbai, +91 20 for Pune) builds local credibility.</li>
  <li><strong>UPI payment integration:</strong> UPI is as dominant in Maharashtra as across India — PhonePe, Google Pay, and Paytm are all widely used. For any e-commerce or payment capability, UPI support is non-negotiable.</li>
  <li><strong>Social media:</strong> Instagram and YouTube (in Marathi) are growing rapidly as content discovery platforms for Maharashtra audiences. A Marathi-language YouTube channel ranks well for Marathi searches and builds brand credibility.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

{% block section_4_2 %}
<p>
  Maharashtra's mobile internet landscape varies significantly between Mumbai/Pune (fast 4G/5G, high smartphone sophistication) and rural Maharashtra (variable connectivity, more affordable devices).
</p>
<ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px;">
  <li><strong>Mumbai and Pune:</strong> Jio's cheap data plans have made fast mobile internet accessible across income brackets. Richer web experiences work in metro Maharashtra — but performance still matters as a baseline quality signal.</li>
  <li><strong>Rural Maharashtra:</strong> Farmers and smaller city residents may be on 3G networks with more affordable Android devices. If your audience extends beyond metros, optimize for this segment's constraints.</li>
  <li><strong>Devanagari input on mobile:</strong> Marathi keyboard input on mobile requires either a Devanagari keyboard or transliteration input. Many users prefer reading Marathi but typing in English — consider whether your forms need Marathi input specifically.</li>
  <li><strong>UPI click-to-pay deep links:</strong> For checkout flows, UPI deep links that launch payment apps directly are the smoothest mobile payment experience for Indian users.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}

